    "lawCode": "Add Art 8 Title 34 §§2799-aaa - 2799-zzz, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3250\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nto amend the public authorities law, in relation to creating the\nSyracuse regional airport authority\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo create a Syracuse regional airport authority.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the State public authorities law to add a new\nSyracuse Regional Airport Authority. The authority shall constitute a\npublic benefit corporation and shall consist of eleven members who\nshall be appointed by the Mayor of Syracuse, the Onondaga County\nExecutive and various local officials. In addition this legislation\nauthorizes the following:\n\n* the authority shall have the power to borrow money and issue bonds;\n* to appoint officers, employees and agents as the authority may\nrequire for the performance of its duties;\n* establish fixed, revised fees and collect fares, rentals, rates,\ncharges, landing and field use fees, concession fees and other fees\nas it may deem necessary, convenient or desirable for the use and\noperation of any real property, aviation facilities and pollution\ncontrol facilities managed by the authority;\n* New York State and City of Syracuse shall not impair the rights and\nremedies of the holders of bonds issued by the authority;\n* the authority shall be exempt from taxes, assessments and certain\nfees; and\n* except in action for wrongful death, no action or special\nproceeding shall be prosecuted or maintained against the authority.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe economic well-being of the state and the general welfare of its\npeople require adequate, safe, secure and efficient aviation and\ntransportation facilities at a reasonable cost to the people.\nTherefore, strengthening and improving aviation facilities for the\ncentral part of the state is a matter of vital importance not only to\nthe residents of central New York but to all the state's residents.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall be effective immediately.\n\n\n",
